# Stack

```
Mogged.app (Swift desktop) → hidden runtime → Wine + DXVK/vkd3d-proton + MoltenVK → Metal
```

The desktop app is the product. Keep the execution backend **swappable** (`dxvk-moltenvk` | `vkd3d-moltenvk` | `moltenvk`). Do not hardcode a vendor toolkit path in the launcher. Do not design UI around a toolkit. Zero paid software.

## Graphics

- Spider-Man Remastered is **D3D12**. DXVK will not translate it. Use vkd3d-proton → MoltenVK.
- DLSS does not exist here. Use FSR in-game and/or MetalFX. Ray tracing off unless a benchmark says otherwise.
- Title-specific env and upscaler choices belong in `profiles/*.json`, not in Swift.

## Process

Launcher passes profile id + install path. Runtime creates, launches, kills, and logs. The user never configures an isolated Windows environment.
